## Root Cause

The coding agent's `edit_file` tool always reads the file before editing. When the file doesn't exist, GitHub returns 404 → the `/file-content` endpoint swallowed it as a generic 500 → the agent saw `"Failed to read file"` and gave up.

## Three fixes (3 files changed)

**`backend/src/routes/landingPageGeneration.ts`**
- `/file-content` endpoint now returns `404 { error: "File not found", newFile: true }` when the file doesn't exist on the branch **or** on main, instead of converting it to a 500.

**`backend/src/services/codingAgentService.ts`**
- `edit_file` tool now wraps the pre-read in a try/catch: a 404 is treated as empty content, so the agent can proceed to create the file.
- `applySearchReplace` supports `{ search: "", replace: "<full content>" }` on empty content as a file-creation idiom.
- System prompt updated to tell the agent it can create new files and how.

**`backend/src/__tests__/codingAgentService.test.ts`**
- 3 new tests: line-edit on empty file, empty-search create, empty-search rejected on non-empty file. All 49 tests pass.

## Immediate unblock

Lyndi's Every.io landing pages can now have the CORS proxy route `app/api/leads/route.ts` created directly by the coding agent.

